Subject: [PATCH 10/32] fix(desktop): touch-reachable TERMINAL close + drawer
 touch fixes + drag-follow
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

F4c: coarse pointers get a 44px collapse button in tool-panel zone headers
(the terminal strip the user could not close on phones); it routes through
the pane's registered closer, so hermes.desktop.terminalTakeover flips to
false and survives restarts. The narrow drawers stop registering hover
strips on touch, always render a backdrop, and gain a 44px close button;
drawers now expose data-narrow-drawer-pane so edge-swipe closes route to
the revealed pane's id.

F4f: edge swipes are side-aware (right drawer mirrors left) and follow the
finger — drawerDragProgress/drawerReleaseDecision pure math drives a
$drawerDrag atom the overlay renders from, mounting the pane at gesture
start with translateX/opacity tracking; release settles through a 160ms
transition (snap open, spring back, never jump). All listeners stay
passive; the vertical-scroll abstain is unchanged.
